  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; only governmental funds (School Nutrition is a special revenue fund, so no business-type funds). Receipts and disbursements from Exhibit D total column (p4). Beginning cash = beginning fund balances 4,286,013 (p4); ending cash = total assets/fund balances 4,563,901 (p3) incl. 1,223,518 cash with fiscal agent. Local Sources split by category using the fund schedules (pp5,7,8,9,10); splits sum to 5,126,463 and tie to Exhibit B property tax, carline, interest. County and State Sources kept as printed (State includes homestead/property tax credit and nameplate capacity tax; the General fund detail marks nameplate as other taxes). Debt Service 262,376 split using Special Building schedule (245,000 principal; 17,126 interest + 250 other). Transfers 732,331 in and out (General Fund transfers out to Nutrition 82,331, Activities 150,000, Depreciation 500,000); not included in spending lines. Detail uses the fund budget schedules only (no more detailed schedules exist); General Fund spending is by function only (not itemized); 2650 Vehicle Acquisition and Absorb Unused Budget Authority have zero actuals and are omitted; General Fund Total Disbursements and Transfers 8,043,042 on p6 (printed) vs 7,310,711+732,331=8,043,042. Exhibit B statement of activities has no separate business-type activities. Balance sheet from Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis (Exhibit A, p1); no liabilities. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
